  "title": "datasette-cluster-map 0.19",
  "summary": "Release: datasette-cluster-map 0.19 One of the oldest Datasette plugins, and still one of my favorites. It now works with Datasette 1.0a42, and depends on the new datasette-leaflet to ensure OpenStreetMap tiles are requested with a referrer header. Here's a map of power plants owned by California's PG&E , also demonstrating Datasette's recently redesigned f…",
  "content": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/datasette-cluster-map/releases/tag/0.19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">datasette-cluster-map 0.19</a></p>\n        <p>One of the oldest Datasette plugins, and still one of my favorites. It now works with Datasette 1.0a42, and depends on <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/13/datasette-leaflet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">the new datasette-leaflet</a> to ensure OpenStreetMap tiles are requested with a referrer header.</p>\n<p>Here&#x27;s <a href=\"https://datasette.io/global-power-plants/global-power-plants?owner=Pacific+Gas+%26+Electric+Co.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">a map of power plants owned by California&#x27;s PG&amp;E</a>, also demonstrating Datasette&#x27;s recently <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/datasette/pull/3032\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">redesigned facets</a>:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Screenshot of a faceted map interface. Three facet panels at the top: &quot;country_long 1&quot; with United States of America 81 selected; &quot;owner 1&quot; with Pacific Gas &amp; Electric Co. 81 selected; &quot;primary_fuel 5&quot; listing Hydro 63, Solar 10, Gas 5, Storage 2, Nuclear 1. Each primary_fuel row has a pale blue horizontal bar behind its label, sized in proportion to its count: Hydro&#x27;s bar fills most of the row width, Solar&#x27;s is a short sliver, Gas&#x27;s is shorter still, and Storage and Nuclear have only a thin strip at the left edge. Below is a Leaflet map with + and − zoom controls showing California and Nevada, with marker clusters across northern and central California: 9 near Redding, 21 near Chico, 2 to the west of Chico, 13 northeast of Sacramento, 7 east of Stockton, 6 at Oakland, 10 at Fresno, 9 west of Visalia, 2 north of Bakersfield, plus two individual blue pin markers on the coast, one in the far north and one north of Santa Maria. Attribution: Leaflet | © OpenStreetMap contributors\" src=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/power-plants-pge.webp\"></p>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">datasette</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/geospatial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">geospatial</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/openstreetmap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">openstreetmap</a></p>",
  "image": "https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/power-plants-pge.webp",
